Subject: Re: Unable to open an initial console on Alphastation 200
In-Reply-To: <199702052347.PAA06110@draco.acs.uci.edu>

[...]
>>   Unable to open a initial console
[...]

  Your /dev is most likely empty. It must at least contain "tty0" and
"tty1" (if I remember correctly) to allow an initial process to be fired
up by the kernel, and "zero" to allow ELF binaries to run since ld.so
wants to mmap it.

