Subject: Re: Fwd: [RELEASED] Kaffe 0.8.0
In-Reply-To: <v02130505af250fbe4bb6@[140.254.85.2]>

> /tmp/cca17078.s: Assembler messages:
> /tmp/cca17078.s:14808: Error: opcode `amask' not supported for target <all>
> /tmp/cca17078.s:15117: Error: opcode `amask' not supported for target <all>

Either get a new assembler or edit config/alpha/jit-alpha.def,
search for amask, and switch the #if 1 there to #if 0.

That is an odd looking message, though.  What version of gas is it?  It
seems to think it knows what amask is, though it won't let you use it.

BTW, Tim changed bits of the struct thread layout at the last minute
that affected some offsets hardcoded in some assembly.  Here is a 
patch that gets rid of the hardcoding.

  ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/alphabits/kaffe-0.8.0-axp-970210.diff

r~

