I don't know that anyone has ever tried.  There is a JDK on gatekeeper for
Digital Unix 3.2.  Digital Unix has some thread system calls that I am not
sure have Linux equivalents.  Java may use some of them which would be
problematic, but I am just speculating.  I forget who did the JDK port for
Digital, but it is one of the same people who is working on Linux/Alpha,
so perhaps they will enlighten us.

